.TH GIT-DIFF-COMMITS 1 "2026-10-01" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-diff-commits \- compare two commits side by side
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git diff-commits
.IR COMMIT1 COMMIT2
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-diff-commits\fR opens a side-by-side diff between two commits using
\fBgit difftool --no-index\fR. This is useful for reviewing what changed between
revisions without leaving the terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git diff-commits HEAD~3 HEAD
Compare the current branch tip to the commit three revisions earlier.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-difftool (1)
